This chapter shares only duel, Combat, fighter, roster, Team, count, reporting, decided, seeded, biding, enlist, heal, calm, recalculate, teach, challenge, confront, encounter, fight, respond, roll, announce, report, proceed, experience needed and capacity.

Use the foundation, sound, cries, learnsets, encounters and matchups chapters.

A fighter has a first form (text), a species (text), a level (number), an experience (number), a health (number), a maximum health (number), an attack (number), a defense (number), a special (number), a speed (number), a moves (list of text), a pp (list of numbers), a status (text), an attack stage (number), a defense stage (number), a speed stage (number), an accuracy stage (number), a bide turns (number) and a stored damage (number).
A fighter can be seeded.
A fighter is biding when its bide turns is more than 0.
Let the statuses always be a list of "", "poisoned", "burned" and "paralyzed".
A fighter's status is always in the statuses.
There is a fighter called Empty Ally whose first form is "", whose species is "", whose level is 0, whose experience is 0, whose health is 0, whose maximum health is 1, whose attack is 1, whose defense is 1, whose special is 1, whose speed is 1, whose status is "", whose attack stage is 0, whose defense stage is 0, whose speed stage is 0, whose accuracy stage is 0, whose bide turns is 0 and whose stored damage is 0.
There is a fighter called Empty Foe whose first form is "", whose species is "", whose level is 0, whose experience is 0, whose health is 0, whose maximum health is 1, whose attack is 1, whose defense is 1, whose special is 1, whose speed is 1, whose status is "", whose attack stage is 0, whose defense stage is 0, whose speed stage is 0, whose accuracy stage is 0, whose bide turns is 0 and whose stored damage is 0.

A side is one of ally or foe.

A duel has an ally (fighter), a foe (fighter), a challenger (text), a trainer (text), a foe position (number), a trainer full heals (number), an active (number), an outcome (text), a message (text), a later lines (list of text), a choice (number), a turn (number) and a seed (number).
There is a duel called Combat whose ally is Empty Ally, whose foe is Empty Foe, whose challenger is "", whose trainer is "", whose foe position is 0, whose trainer full heals is 0, whose active is 0, whose outcome is "", whose message is "", whose choice is 1, whose turn is 0 and whose seed is 47.
A roster has a members (list of fighters), a selected (number), a result (text) and a notice (text).
There is a roster called Team whose selected is 1 and whose result is "" and whose notice is "".
The count of a roster is the number of items in its members.

A duel is reporting when the number of items in its later lines is more than 0.
A duel is decided when its ally's health is less than 1 or its foe's health is less than 1.

